  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "goal",
      "title": "Lesson Goals",
      "items": [
        "Talk about your daily routine using reflexive and regular verbs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "grammar-inline",
      "title": "Reflexive Verbs",
      "html": "<p>Many daily activities in Spanish use <strong>reflexive verbs</strong>. These describe things you do <em>to yourself</em>.</p><p>You add <strong>me</strong> before the verb:</p><p>levantarse → <strong>me levanto</strong><br>\"to get up\" → \"I get up\"</p><p>ducharse → <strong>me ducho</strong><br>\"to shower\" → \"I shower\"</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "example-inline",
      "title": "A Morning Routine",
      "html": "<p><strong>Me levanto</strong> a las siete.<br><em>I get up at seven.</em></p><p><strong>Me ducho</strong> y <strong>me visto</strong>.<br><em>I shower and get dressed.</em></p><p><strong>Desayuno</strong> café con tostadas.<br><em>I have coffee and toast for breakfast.</em></p>"
    },
